+# build labelled journal positions, so the agent saw gaps (obs-1, obs-2, obs-4) and the first live v2 run's Mechanic read the
+# gap as a missing observation. Now such an observation gets no label, the labels the agent sees are obs-1..obs-n with no
+# gaps, each keeps its label on later turns, and only a label that was shown is decoded; any other token (obs-4 below, or
+# any guess) stays as written and fails the evidence check (C6) exactly as in v1, where a hidden ID cannot be guessed.
 
